    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d312">

                <pb facs="0493" n="417" xml:id="pg417"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">548.D1/208: Circular instruction</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to American Diplomatic
                        Representatives in South America</hi><anchor n="66" xml:id="d312-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-02-12">February 12, 1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sirs</hi>: The Department has been informed by High
                    Commissioner James G. McDonald, representing the High Commission for Refugees
                    (Jewish and others) Coming from Germany, and Mr. Samuel Guy Inman, that they are
                    about to visit various countries of South America listed in the enclosed
                    itinerary to treat with them concerning the entrance of some of the refugees
                    into those countries.</p>
                <p>You will please extend appropriate courtesies to these gentlemen, bearing in
                    mind, however, that they do not represent the United States. There is enclosed
                    for your information a memorandum<anchor n="67" xml:id="d312-f2"/> concerning
                    the High Commission and this Government’s relation to it.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William
                            Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d312-f1" n="66" type="source" xml:id="d312-f1-content">
                <p>Also sent to the Consular Officer at Guayaquil.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d312-f2" n="67" xml:id="d312-f2-content">
